---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import TableWrap from '../components/TableWrap.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';

const profileJson = `{
  "user_profile": {
    "interview_completed": true,
    "code_literacy": "basic",
    "autonomy": "collaborative",
    "pr_review": "walkthrough",
    "verbosity": "detailed",
    "gamification_preference": "light",
    "learning": "teach",
    "risk_tolerance": "balanced",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-04T14:32:15Z"
  }
}`;
---

<DocsLayout title="Personalization" sectionLabel="How It Works" activeSlug="personalization">

  <div class="toc">
    <h3>On This Page</h3>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#overview">How the Profile System Works</a></li>
      <li><a href="#dimensions">Dimensions</a></li>
      <li><a href="#interview">The Profile Interview</a></li>
      <li><a href="#agent-adaptation">How Agents Adapt</a></li>
      <li><a href="#storage">Storage &amp; Scripts</a></li>
      <li><a href="#changing">Changing Your Profile</a></li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <!-- ── Overview ── -->
  <section class="section" id="overview">
    <div class="panel-intro">
      <h2>How the Profile System Works</h2>
      <p>Most AI coding tools treat every user the same. A non-technical founder gets the same unexplained terminal output as a senior developer. A learner is overwhelmed by terse error messages. An experienced developer wades through verbose explanations they don't need. VibeCrew's profile system solves this by adapting <strong>every agent's behavior</strong> to your experience level, working style, and preferences.</p>
      <div class="key-points">
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What it is</strong>
            <p>A multi-dimension preference system that controls how every agent communicates, how much autonomy the system takes, how technical the language is, and how adventurous technology choices are.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>What problem it solves</strong>
            <p>A founder who can't read code needs walkthrough PRs with plain English. A senior developer wants minimal output and full autonomy. The profile ensures both get exactly the experience they need &mdash; without either having to fight the defaults.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="key-point">
          <span class="key-icon amber">&#9888;</span>
          <div>
            <strong>Completely optional</strong>
            <p>If you skip the profile interview, every agent uses sensible defaults (checkpoints autonomy, standard verbosity, balanced risk). You can run <code>/profile</code> at any time &mdash; or change settings directly in the dashboard.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ── The 7 Dimensions ── -->
  <section class="section" id="dimensions">
    <h3>Dimensions</h3>
    <p>Each dimension controls a different axis of the system's behavior. Together they create a unique experience tailored to your needs.</p>

    <div class="dimension-cards">
      <div class="dimension-card">
        <div class="dimension-header">
          <span class="dimension-icon">&#128214;</span>
          <h4>Code Literacy</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="dimension-desc">How technical the language in reviews, errors, docs, and commit messages is.</p>
        <div class="dimension-options">
          <span class="option"><strong>Fluent</strong> &mdash; technical jargon used freely, minimal comments</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Conversational</strong> &mdash; brief definitions for domain jargon</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Basic</strong> &mdash; plain English comments on exports and complex logic</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>None</strong> &mdash; every export gets JSDoc, error messages include plain-language explanations</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dimension-card">
        <div class="dimension-header">
          <span class="dimension-icon">&#127918;</span>
          <h4>Autonomy</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="dimension-desc">How much VibeCrew does on its own before asking for approval.</p>
        <div class="dimension-options">
          <span class="option"><strong>Full Auto</strong> &mdash; make decisions and keep going, only stop when blocked</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Checkpoints</strong> &mdash; check in at major decisions (tech stack, design, merge)</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Collaborative</strong> &mdash; explain each step, user understands and approves</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Supervised</strong> &mdash; ask before every significant action, full control</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dimension-card">
        <div class="dimension-header">
          <span class="dimension-icon">&#128203;</span>
          <h4>PR Review</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="dimension-desc">How code changes are packaged and merged.</p>
        <div class="dimension-options">
          <span class="option"><strong>Auto-merge</strong> &mdash; merge after tests pass, skip PRs entirely</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Summary</strong> &mdash; PR with a brief 3-line summary</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Review</strong> &mdash; detailed PR with quality gate table and test plan</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Walkthrough</strong> &mdash; line-by-line explanations of every change</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dimension-card">
        <div class="dimension-header">
          <span class="dimension-icon">&#128172;</span>
          <h4>Verbosity</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="dimension-desc">How much detail you get in messages, coaching, and session summaries.</p>
        <div class="dimension-options">
          <span class="option"><strong>Minimal</strong> &mdash; just the facts: status, errors, done</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Standard</strong> &mdash; brief explanations of what happened and what's next</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Detailed</strong> &mdash; decisions, trade-offs, and alternatives explained</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Educational</strong> &mdash; teaches concepts and patterns as you go</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dimension-card">
        <div class="dimension-header">
          <span class="dimension-icon">&#127942;</span>
          <h4>Gamification</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="dimension-desc">How much of the progression system (XP, badges, streaks) is visible.</p>
        <div class="dimension-options">
          <span class="option"><strong>All In</strong> &mdash; show everything: XP, levels, badges, streaks, challenges</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Light Touch</strong> &mdash; show level and score, skip badges/streaks</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Score Only</strong> &mdash; just the Vibe Score, nothing else</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Disabled</strong> &mdash; no gamification output at all</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dimension-card">
        <div class="dimension-header">
          <span class="dimension-icon">&#127891;</span>
          <h4>Learning Style</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="dimension-desc">How the system helps you understand your project's codebase.</p>
        <div class="dimension-options">
          <span class="option"><strong>Don't Explain</strong> &mdash; just build, user reads the code themselves</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Reference Docs</strong> &mdash; generate documentation to read later</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Inline</strong> &mdash; comments in code, explanations in commits</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Teach Me</strong> &mdash; explain concepts interactively, full understanding</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="dimension-card">
        <div class="dimension-header">
          <span class="dimension-icon">&#9878;</span>
          <h4>Risk Tolerance</h4>
        </div>
        <p class="dimension-desc">How adventurous technology choices are during TDR research.</p>
        <div class="dimension-options">
          <span class="option"><strong>Conservative</strong> &mdash; proven, battle-tested technologies (3+ years, major backing)</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Balanced</strong> &mdash; modern but established, no bleeding-edge or legacy</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Progressive</strong> &mdash; newer technologies if they offer clear advantages</span>
          <span class="option"><strong>Experimental</strong> &mdash; latest and greatest, accepts the risk</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ── The Interview ── -->
  <section class="section" id="interview">
    <h3>The Profile Interview</h3>
    <p>Running <code>/profile</code> starts an interactive interview &mdash; 7 quick questions that take about 2 minutes. The interview is conversational: you can answer with a number (1&ndash;4) or describe what you want in plain text.</p>

    <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Interview Flow</h4>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Question</th><th>Smart Behavior</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>1</strong></td><td>How comfortable are you reading code?</td><td>Calibrates how technical the system's language will be.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>2</strong></td><td>How much should VibeCrew do on its own?</td><td>Controls approval gates across the entire workflow.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>3</strong></td><td>How should code changes be merged?</td><td>Determines PR detail level &mdash; from auto-merge to line-by-line walkthroughs.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>4</strong></td><td>How much detail do you want in messages?</td><td>Affects every agent's output length and explanation depth.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>5</strong></td><td>Do you enjoy gamification?</td><td>Automatically syncs the gamification config (XP display, streak reminders, badges).</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>6</strong></td><td>How do you want to learn about your codebase?</td><td>Controls documentation depth and whether code gets explanatory comments.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>7</strong></td><td>What's your approach to technology choices?</td><td>Steers the Stack Scout toward stable or cutting-edge technologies.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <Callout type="tip" title="Re-run anytime">
      If you already have a profile, <code>/profile</code> shows your current settings first and asks which dimensions you want to change. You don't have to redo the whole interview.
    </Callout>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ── Agent Adaptation ── -->
  <section class="section" id="agent-adaptation">
    <h3>How Agents Adapt</h3>
    <p>Every profile-aware agent calls <code>read-profile.sh</code> on startup to load your preferences. Here's exactly what changes for each agent based on your profile.</p>

    <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Session Startup</h4>
    <p class="cmd-group-desc">Reads <code>verbosity</code> to control greeting depth.</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Verbosity</th><th>Greeting</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Minimal</strong></td><td>4-line banner only. No hints, no handoff summary.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Standard</strong></td><td>Banner + onboarding hint (e.g., "Tip: Run /profile to personalize VibeCrew")</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Detailed</strong></td><td>Banner + hint + one-line project context summary</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Educational</strong></td><td>Banner + hint + context + "Did you know?" tip about unused features</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Workflow Orchestrator</h4>
    <p class="cmd-group-desc">Reads <code>autonomy</code> and <code>verbosity</code> to control approval gates and explanation depth.</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Full Auto</th><th>Checkpoints</th><th>Collaborative</th><th>Supervised</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Foundation artifacts</strong></td><td>Auto-approve all</td><td>Approve per artifact</td><td>Explain then approve</td><td>Show examples, explain reasoning</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>TDR decisions</strong></td><td>Auto-select best</td><td>Recommend + approve</td><td>Side-by-side comparison</td><td>Full debate matrix</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Phase transitions</strong></td><td>Silent</td><td>Announce</td><td>Explain next phase</td><td>Interactive walkthrough</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>/run-backlog pauses</strong></td><td>No pauses</td><td>Pause per feature</td><td>Pause per phase</td><td>Pause per action</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Error recovery</strong></td><td>Auto-fix 3x</td><td>Auto-fix 1x, then ask</td><td>Show error, ask approach</td><td>Explain all options</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Builder</h4>
    <p class="cmd-group-desc">Reads <code>verbosity</code>, <code>code_literacy</code>, and <code>pr_review</code> to shape code output.</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Dimension</th><th>Adaptation</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Commit messages</strong></td><td>verbosity</td><td>Minimal: type(scope) only. Standard: + bullet list. Detailed: + rationale. Educational: + design pattern explanation.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Code comments</strong></td><td>code_literacy</td><td>Fluent: minimal, non-obvious logic only. None: every export gets JSDoc, complex blocks get inline annotations.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>PR body</strong></td><td>pr_review</td><td>Auto-merge: auto-merge label. Summary: 3 lines. Review: full quality gate table. Walkthrough: + per-file code walkthrough.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Verifier</h4>
    <p class="cmd-group-desc">Reads <code>verbosity</code> and <code>gamification_preference</code> for coaching output.</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Dimension</th><th>Adaptation</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>/wrap output</strong></td><td>verbosity</td><td>Minimal: score + rating only. Standard: + coaching suggestions. Detailed: full deduction/bonus breakdown. Educational: + "Learning moment".</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Progression display</strong></td><td>gamification</td><td>Full: XP, levels, badges, streaks, challenges. Light: level + XP only. Score only: Vibe Score. Disabled: no gamification framing.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Stack Scout</h4>
    <p class="cmd-group-desc">Reads <code>risk_tolerance</code> to weight technology maturity in TDR research.</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Risk Tolerance</th><th>Technology Selection Criteria</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Conservative</strong></td><td>3+ years production use, 100k+ npm weekly downloads, major company backing. Exclude technologies under 2 years old.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Balanced</strong></td><td>Modern but established. Standard comparison across maturity, DX, and community.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Progressive</strong></td><td>Consider 1&ndash;2 year old technologies if they offer clear advantages. Include benchmarks.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Experimental</strong></td><td>Seek cutting-edge options. Include alpha/beta-stage technologies. Add "Migration if this fails" section to TDR.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Code Reviewer</h4>
    <p class="cmd-group-desc">Reads <code>code_literacy</code> and <code>pr_review</code> to adjust finding explanations and review thoroughness.</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Dimension</th><th>Adaptation</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Finding language</strong></td><td>code_literacy</td><td>Fluent: technical terminology, brief findings. Conversational: adds context parentheticals. Basic: plain English with before/after. None: non-technical language, grouped by impact.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Review depth</strong></td><td>pr_review</td><td>Auto-merge: critical only (security, correctness). Summary: + light convention check. Review: full 10-step review. Walkthrough: + per-file code walkthrough.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Doc Generator</h4>
    <p class="cmd-group-desc">Reads <code>learning</code> and <code>code_literacy</code> to shape documentation style.</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Dimension</th><th>Adaptation</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Doc depth</strong></td><td>learning</td><td>Don't Explain: minimal maintainability docs. Reference: comprehensive with API references. Inline: + JSDoc flagging. Teach: + "How it works" sections with Mermaid diagrams.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Doc language</strong></td><td>code_literacy</td><td>Fluent: idiomatic code examples. Conversational: parenthetical definitions. Basic: analogies instead of jargon. None: non-technical guide, annotated code.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ── Storage & Scripts ── -->
  <section class="section" id="storage">
    <h3>Storage &amp; Scripts</h3>
    <p>Your profile is stored as JSON in <code>.vibecrew/config.json</code> under the <code>user_profile</code> key. Two bash scripts handle all reads and writes.</p>

    <CodeBlock code={profileJson} lang="json" label=".vibecrew/config.json" />

    <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Profile Scripts</h4>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Script</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Key Behavior</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>read-profile.sh</code></td>
            <td>Universal profile reader called by all agents</td>
            <td>Merges stored profile over defaults so missing fields are always filled. Always exits 0 &mdash; returns defaults if no profile exists. Single bash call, ~500 tokens.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>save-profile.sh</code></td>
            <td>Writes profile and syncs gamification config</td>
            <td>Atomic writes via PID-suffixed temp files. Validates config.json exists. Sets <code>interview_completed: true</code> and <code>updated_at</code> timestamp. Uses advisory locks for concurrent safety.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Gamification Sync</h4>
    <p>When you change the gamification preference, <code>save-profile.sh</code> automatically syncs three related config flags:</p>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Preference</th><th>enabled</th><th>show_xp_in_status</th><th>streak_reminders</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Full</strong></td><td>true</td><td>true</td><td>true</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Light</strong></td><td>true</td><td>true</td><td>false</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Score Only</strong></td><td>true</td><td>false</td><td>false</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Disabled</strong></td><td>false</td><td>false</td><td>false</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr>

  <!-- ── Changing Your Profile ── -->
  <section class="section" id="changing">
    <h3>Changing Your Profile</h3>
    <p>Your profile isn't locked in. As your experience grows and your needs change, you have two ways to update it.</p>

    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h4>CLI: <code>/profile</code></h4>
        <p>Run <code>/profile</code> in any session. If you already have a profile, it shows your current settings and asks which dimensions you want to change. The conversational interview makes it easy to adjust one or all dimensions without starting from scratch.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>Dashboard: Settings Tab</h4>
        <p>Open your project's Vibe Dashboard and navigate to the <strong>Settings</strong> tab. The browser-based editor lets you modify any profile dimension with dropdowns, see the effect immediately, and save. Changes write directly to <code>.vibecrew/config.json</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>Both methods write to the same <code>config.json</code> file. Changes take effect immediately &mdash; the next agent that runs will read your updated preferences.</p>

    <Callout type="tip" title="Evolve over time">
      A learner who started with educational verbosity and collaborative autonomy might switch to standard and checkpoints after a few projects. A founder who initially needed walkthrough PRs might move to summary PRs once they're comfortable with the process. Revisit your profile whenever your workflow feels too noisy or too quiet.
    </Callout>

    <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Example: A Founder's Journey</h4>
    <div class="agent-table-wrap">
      <table class="agent-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Profile Changes</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Week 1</strong></td>
            <td>Autonomy: supervised, Verbosity: educational, PR: walkthrough</td>
            <td>Learning how everything works. Wants full explanations and control.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Month 1</strong></td>
            <td>Autonomy: collaborative, Verbosity: detailed, PR: review</td>
            <td>Understands the workflow. Still wants to approve decisions but doesn't need hand-holding.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Month 3</strong></td>
            <td>Autonomy: checkpoints, Verbosity: standard, PR: summary</td>
            <td>Trusts the system. Only pauses at major decisions. Reads summaries instead of walkthroughs.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Related Pages ── -->
  <section class="section">
    <h3>Related Pages</h3>
    <div class="page-grid">
      <a class="page-card" href="gamification.html">
        <h4>Gamification</h4>
        <p>XP, leveling, badges, skill tree, streaks, challenges, and quizzes that reward good development habits.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View details &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href="agents.html">
        <h4>Sub-Agents</h4>
        <p>The specialized agents that read your profile and adapt their behavior accordingly.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View details &rarr;</span>
      </a>
      <a class="page-card" href="dashboard.html">
        <h4>Vibe Dashboard</h4>
        <p>The browser-based dashboard where you can edit your profile via the Settings tab.</p>
        <span class="card-arrow">View details &rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

</DocsLayout>

